    <item>
      <title>Nevada Governor's Race Is Democrats’ Working-Class Test for 2028</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-31/nevada-governor-s-race-is-democrats-working-class-test-for-2028</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">04f1d5ff95818020ccc5b144</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:14 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>President Donald Trump built his political career on being a working-class whisperer, winning over not only most White voters without four-year college degrees, but significant numbers of blue-collar Latino and Black voters as well. While polls indicate Trump’s Republicans don’t stand a chance of replicating his success in the midterms, this hasn’t quieted the debate among Democrats over how best to out-whisper the whisperer.</description>
      <dc:creator>Erika D. Smith</dc:creator>
